Map data from OpenStreetMap, through Geoapify
---------------------------------------------

Some test fixtures keep small extracts of map data, so that the tests can check places
without calling a live service:

- src/lib/fixtures/places/coverage-run.ts holds Geoapify's geocoding answers for the 66
  places of three hand-written days, recorded on 2026-10-28: each candidate's names, its
  distance, its result type and its category.
  src/lib/fixtures/places/coverage-responses.ts rebuilds geocoding responses from them.
- src/lib/days/written/checks.ts holds the place checks recorded when each of the six
  written days was generated, on 2026-10-31: Geoapify's point and place id for each place
  confirmed by name, and how many places it found around each area checked.
- src/lib/fixtures/curated/kyoto.ts and src/lib/fixtures/curated/lisbon.ts are days
  written by hand whose coordinates come mostly or wholly from OpenStreetMap.

- docs/place-match-audit.md and docs/grounding.md quote some of the same recorded answers
  as evidence: candidate names, distances and match results from the place rounds run
  between 2026-10-28 and 2026-10-31.

