See https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright for the data's sources and licence.
The recorded answers were provided by Geoapify (https://www.geoapify.com), whose services
serve OpenStreetMap data. The MIT License covers the code around this data, not the data.

These look alike but are not recordings: src/lib/fixtures/places/meal-areas.ts,
src/lib/fixtures/intake/places.ts and the samples in src/lib/quality/lost-accents.test.ts
are written by hand in the shapes Geoapify documents,
with made-up ids and, around the meals, made-up businesses.

The site itself credits the same sources on every day: "© OpenStreetMap contributors ·
Powered by Geoapify".


